  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of State has obligated $5.3B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The agency recorded 17,402 awards with an average award size of $303K. Obligations are down 46.6% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations show a peak at $11.9B in FY22, followed by $11.7B in FY23 and FY24, $9.9B in FY25, and $5.3B in FY26 to date. Contract spending concentrates in services and finance related sectors. Security Guards and Patrol Services accounts for $794M, Other Computer Related Services accounts for $667M, and Computer Systems Design Services accounts for $553M. The vendor list is topped by CGI FEDERAL INC. with $223M, followed by CITIBANK, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION with $159M, and INTER-CON SECURITY SYSTEMS, INC. with $148M. The FY2026 to date mix reflects continued demand for security, IT services, and facilities and financial services, while overall obligations are materially lower than full prior-year totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Department of State contract spending changed year over year?",
        "body": "The Department of State obligated $5.3B in FY2026 to date, down 46.6% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations were $9.5B in FY21, $11.9B in FY22, $11.7B in FY23, $11.7B in FY24, and $9.9B in FY25. The current-year total is partial because FY2026 to date figures cover the fiscal year to date. Award activity totaled 17,402 awards in FY2026 to date with an average award size of $303K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What product and vendor categories are largest for State in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Security Guards and Patrol Services is the largest NAICS category at $794M, followed by Other Computer Related Services at $667M and Computer Systems Design Services at $553M. Facilities Support Services accounts for $321M, Computer Facilities Management Services accounts for $295M, and Commercial Banking accounts for $293M. CGI FEDERAL INC. is the top vendor at $223M, followed by CITIBANK, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION at $159M and INTER-CON SECURITY SYSTEMS, INC. at $148M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of State spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of State has obligated $5.3B on contracts in FY2026 to date. The agency recorded 17,402 awards with an average award size of $303K. Obligations are down 46.6% year over year and the current-year total is partial because fiscal year to date figures are reported."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does State buy?",
      "a": "State buys security services, IT services, consulting, facilities support, and banking services. Security Guards and Patrol Services accounts for $794M, Other Computer Related Services accounts for $667M, Computer Systems Design Services accounts for $553M, Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services accounts for $405M, Facilities Support Services accounts for $321M, and Commercial Banking accounts for $293M."
    },
